  "resume": "This is a Swiss TV news report from the Tagesschau series broadcast on 8 May 1965, covering commemorations of the 20th anniversary of Germany's surrender in World War II across multiple European capitals. It shows official ceremonies in Paris, Bonn, East Berlin, and Prague, featuring state leaders such as Heinrich Lübke, Ludwig Erhard, Walter Ulbricht, Alexej Kossygin, and Jozef Cyrankiewicz."
